      "text": "To solve the equation \\( 7^{x+7} = 8^x \\), we will start by expressing both sides of the equation with the same base. However, since the bases are different (7 and 8), we will use logarithms to help us. We can take the natural logarithm (or any logarithm, but we'll use natural logarithm for convenience) of both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\ln(7^{x+7}) = \\ln(8^x)\n\\]\n\nUsing the logarithm power rule, \\(\\ln(a^b) = b\\ln(a)\\), we can rewrite the equation as:\n\n\\[\n(x+7)\\ln(7) = x\\ln(8)\n\\]\n\nNext, we expand and rearrange the equation to isolate \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx\\ln(7) + 7\\ln(7) = x\\ln(8)\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx\\ln(7) - x\\ln(8) = -7\\ln(7)\n\\]\n\nFactor out \\(x\\) on the left side:\n\n\\[\nx(\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)) = -7\\ln(7)\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides by \\(\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-7\\ln(7)}{\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify the expression \\(\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)\\) using the properties of logarithms:\n\n\\[\n\\ln(7) - \\ln(8) = \\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right)\n\\]\n\nSo the expression for \\(x\\) becomes:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-7\\ln(7)}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right)}\n\\]\n\nTo express \\(x\\) in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we observe that:\n\n\\[\nx = \\log_b 7^7 = \\frac{\\ln(7^7)}{\\ln(b)} = \\frac{7\\ln(7)}{\\ln(b)}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(x = \\frac{-7\\ln(7)}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right)}\\), we can equate the two expressions for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{7\\ln(7)}{\\ln(b)} = \\frac{-7\\ln(7)}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right)}\n\\]\n\nBy canceling \\(7\\ln(7)\\) from both sides (assuming \\(\\ln(7) \\neq 0\\)):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\ln(b)} = \\frac{-1}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right)}\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\ln(b) = -\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right)\n\\]\n\nUsing the property of logarithms that \\(-\\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right) = \\ln\\left(\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)^{-1}\\right) = \\ln\\left(\\frac{7}{8}\\right)^{-1}\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\ln(b) = \\ln\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)\n\\]\n\nSince the logarithms are equal, we can conclude that:\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{8}{7}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(b\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{8}{7}}\n\\]",
