      "text": "   - To solve the equation \\(7^{x+7} = 8^x\\) and express the solution in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we start by taking the natural logarithm (or any logarithm) of both sides of the equation. Let's use the natural logarithm for convenience.\n\n   \\[\n   \\ln(7^{x+7}) = \\ln(8^x)\n   \\]\n\n   Using the properties of logarithms, we can rewrite the equation as:\n\n   \\[\n   (x+7) \\ln 7 = x \\ln 8\n   \\]\n\n   Next, we distribute the logarithms:\n\n   \\[\n   x \\ln 7 + 7 \\ln 7 = x \\ln 8\n   \\]\n\n   To isolate \\(x\\), we rearrange the terms:\n\n   \\[\n   x \\ln 7 - x \\ln 8 = -7 \\ln 7\n   \\]\n\n   Factor out \\(x\\) on the left side:\n\n   \\[\n   x (\\ln 7 - \\ln 8) = -7 \\ln 7\n   \\]\n\n   Solve for \\(x\\):\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{-7 \\ln 7}{\\ln 7 - \\ln 8}\n   \\]\n\n   We can simplify the expression by recognizing that \\(\\ln 8 = \\ln (2^3) = 3 \\ln 2\\). Therefore, the equation becomes:\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{-7 \\ln 7}{\\ln 7 - 3 \\ln 2}\n   \\]\n\n   To express \\(x\\) in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we need to rewrite \\(x\\) in terms of base 10 or natural logarithms. Notice that:\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\log_8 7^7\n   \\]\n\n   Using the change of base formula for logarithms, \\(\\log_b a = \\frac{\\log_c a}{\\log_c b}\\), we can rewrite \\(x\\) as:\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{\\log_2 7^7}{\\log_2 8}\n   \\]\n\n   Since \\(\\log_2 8 = \\log_2 (2^3) = 3\\), we have:\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7 \\log_2 7}{3}\n   \\]\n\n   Recognizing that \\(\\log_2 7 = \\frac{\\ln 7}{\\ln 2}\\), we get:\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7 \\frac{\\ln 7}{\\ln 2}}{3} = \\frac{7 \\ln 7}{3 \\ln 2}\n   \\]\n\n   Comparing this with \\(\\log_8 7^7 = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 / 8\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 \\cdot 2^{-3}\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 / 8\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 \\cdot 2^{-3}\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 / 8\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 / 8\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 / 8\\right)\\), we see that:\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 / 8\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 \\cdot 2^{-3}\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 \\cdot 2^{-3}\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 / 8\\right) = \\log_2 \\left(7^7 / 8\\right)\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, \\(b = 2\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
